#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:44
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Tar"
msgstr "Instalação do Tar"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:46
#, xml-text
msgid "Prepare Tar for compilation:"
msgstr "Prepare o Tar para compilação:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:48
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"configure\">FORCE_UNSAFE_CONFIGURE=1  \\\n"
"./configure --prefix=/usr</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"configure\">FORCE_UNSAFE_CONFIGURE=1  \\\n"
"./configure --prefix=/usr</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:52
#, xml-text
msgid "The meaning of the configure option:"
msgstr "O significado da opção de configure:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:55
#, xml-text
msgid "<envar>FORCE_UNSAFE_CONFIGURE=1</envar>"
msgstr "<envar>FORCE_UNSAFE_CONFIGURE=1</envar>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:57
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This forces the test for <function>mknod</function> to be run as <systemitem"
" class=\"username\">root</systemitem>.  It is generally considered dangerous"
" to run this test as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user, but as it is being run on a system that has only been partially built,"
" overriding it is OK."
msgstr ""
"Isso força o teste para <function>mknod</function> ser executado como "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>. Geralmente é considerado "
"perigoso executar esse teste como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, porém, como ele está sendo executado "
"em um sistema que foi construído somente parcialmente, substitui-lo está OK."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:67
#, xml-text
msgid "Compile the package:"
msgstr "Compile o pacote:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:69
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"make\">make</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"make\">make</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:71
#, xml-text
msgid "To test the results, issue:"
msgstr "Para testar os resultados, emita:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:73
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"test\">make check</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"test\">make check</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:75
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"One test, capabilities: binary store/restore, is known to fail if it is run "
"because LFS lacks selinux, but will be skipped if the host kernel does not "
"support extended attributes or security labels on the filesystem used for "
"building LFS."
msgstr ""
"Um teste, \"capabilities: binary store/restore\", é conhecido por falhar se "
"for executado, pois o LFS carece de \"selinux\"; porém, será pulado se o "
"núcleo do anfitrião não suportar atributos estendidos ou rótulos de "
"segurança no sistema de arquivos usado para construir o LFS."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:80
#, xml-text
msgid "Install the package:"
msgstr "Instale o pacote:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/tar.xml:82
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"install\">make install\n"
"make -C doc install-html docdir=/usr/share/doc/tar-&tar-version;</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"install\">make install\n"
"make -C doc install-html docdir=/usr/share/doc/tar-&tar-version;</userinput>"

